<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Linux on A Moment's Rest</title><link>https://a-moment096.github.io/en/tags/linux/</link><description>Recent content in Linux on A Moment's Rest</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 26 Jun 2026 15:20:58 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://a-moment096.github.io/en/tags/linux/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Setting Up Ubuntu WSL for Machine Learning</title><link>https://a-moment096.github.io/en/posts/others/wsl_ubuntu_config/</link><pubDate>Sat, 29 Nov 2025 14:28:17 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://a-moment096.github.io/en/posts/others/wsl_ubuntu_config/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://a-moment096.github.io/images/%E3%83%94%E3%83%B3%E3%82%AF%E3%81%AE%E5%A4%A2.png" alt="Featured image of post Setting Up Ubuntu WSL for Machine Learning" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Someone needed to set up an environment for machine learning. This is what happened to his computer after setting it up&amp;hellip;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The header image features an adorable sheep, from &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.pixiv.net/artworks/112910033#1" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;ピンクの夢&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.pixiv.net/users/3402557" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;Ruziかねつカーぺット&lt;/a&gt;. Pink and cute~&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The track is &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1j3411L76S/" title="Original Bilibili link"
 target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;さよならプリンセス&lt;/a&gt; (Goodbye Princess) from &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1924y1T7mV/" title="Bilibili link"
 target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;STUDY WITH MIKU -part2-&lt;/a&gt;, originally by producer &lt;a class="link" href="https://twitter.com/kaivcl" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;Kai&lt;/a&gt;, sung by Hatsune Miku. Playful music, so nice&amp;hellip;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Syncing with rsync</title><link>https://a-moment096.github.io/en/posts/shell_note/use_rsync/</link><pubDate>Mon, 28 Jul 2025 12:43:39 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://a-moment096.github.io/en/posts/shell_note/use_rsync/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://a-moment096.github.io/images/%E8%B4%9D%E5%8A%A0%E5%B0%94%E6%B9%96%E7%95%94.jpg" alt="Featured image of post Syncing with rsync" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Kinda getting tired of &lt;code&gt;scp&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;sftp&lt;/code&gt;. Maybe I&amp;rsquo;ve just been using them wrong, but either way, I&amp;rsquo;m going with &lt;code&gt;rsync&lt;/code&gt;!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;del&gt;Couldn&amp;rsquo;t find the source for this image&amp;hellip; Snagged it from a friend &amp;ndash; it&amp;rsquo;s gorgeous, so I put it here.&lt;/del&gt; Found it! It&amp;rsquo;s by &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.pixiv.net/en/users/8605991" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;fasnakegod&lt;/a&gt; &amp;ndash; &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.pixiv.net/en/artworks/125739568" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;Lake Baikal&lt;/a&gt;. With that, let me share a piano piece. Here&amp;rsquo;s &lt;strong&gt;Kishi Ou no Hokori&lt;/strong&gt; (The Pride of the Knight King) for you all. (Totally unrelated, come on!) *&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>What Was the Last Command?</title><link>https://a-moment096.github.io/en/posts/shell_note/last_command/</link><pubDate>Sat, 26 Jul 2025 20:09:18 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://a-moment096.github.io/en/posts/shell_note/last_command/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://a-moment096.github.io/images/SEASIDE_SOLILOQUIES.png" alt="Featured image of post What Was the Last Command?" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;I used to always wonder: how do you get the previous command? Should be simple, right? After a quick search, here&amp;rsquo;s what I found. Let me jot it down.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The header image is from Orangestar&amp;rsquo;s album &lt;strong&gt;SEASIDE SOLILOQUIES&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;ndash; beautiful art and great music. So for the track pick here, let&amp;rsquo;s go with the title song from that album: &lt;strong&gt;Alice in Reitouko&lt;/strong&gt; (Alice in the Freezer). Hope you enjoy it.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Setting Up an FRP Service</title><link>https://a-moment096.github.io/en/posts/tools_note/frp_depoly/</link><pubDate>Wed, 23 Jul 2025 13:26:16 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://a-moment096.github.io/en/posts/tools_note/frp_depoly/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://a-moment096.github.io/images/BagPipe.jpg" alt="Featured image of post Setting Up an FRP Service" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Why do I have to first ToDesk into a Windows machine, and then SSH from that machine into the server just to connect!? Unbearable. Let&amp;rsquo;s just set up an FRP service myself.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The image features the lovely Ms. Bagpipe. According to unverified sources, it&amp;rsquo;s likely drawn by artist &lt;a class="link" href="https://weibo.com/u/5979033109" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;Liyu黎&lt;/a&gt; as a celebratory illustration for the 2022 Ambience Synesthesia concert. To match, let&amp;rsquo;s play Ms. Bagpipe&amp;rsquo;s personal EP: 《故乡的风》 (Wind of Home).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Installing Arch Linux on a Laptop (Physical Machine)</title><link>https://a-moment096.github.io/en/posts/others/arch_on_laptop/</link><pubDate>Fri, 02 May 2025 16:12:04 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://a-moment096.github.io/en/posts/others/arch_on_laptop/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://a-moment096.github.io/images/Alice.png" alt="Featured image of post Installing Arch Linux on a Laptop (Physical Machine)" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Installing Arch Linux on a virtual machine before was just not satisfying enough (lol, you didn&amp;rsquo;t even finish the series (x)), so this time I&amp;rsquo;m putting Arch on my little thin-and-light. And along the way, documenting the pitfalls you might hit on real hardware?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The header image is from R Sound Design&amp;rsquo;s new track 《アリス？》, a really cheerful Vocaloid song~ Bilibili &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1UtV5zqEjC/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;submission&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/aplayer/dist/APlayer.min.css"&gt;
